  "description": "Wi-Fi data logger with analog and digital channels, buzzer and digital output, readable over Modbus TCP: channel values and status, min/max, pulse counter, battery and supply, logging status, alarm setpoints, clock and network status",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-10-31",
  "firmware": "Instruction manual V3.3x C",
  "source": "Novus LogBox Wi-Fi instruction manual V3.3x C (Portuguese), chapter 9",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "LogBox Wi-Fi - Manual de Instruções",
      "version": "V3.3x C",
      "url": "https://github.com/user-attachments/files/34218860/Manual_LogBox_Wi-Fi_PT.pdf",
      "note": "linked in issue #88; chapter 9, tables 9-11"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus TCP server over Wi-Fi, up to 4 clients at once. Enable it and set the TCP port in NXperience; the map assumes port 502. Any unit id from 0 to 255 is answered.",
    "Functions 03, 06 and 16. Only the buzzer (68) and the clock (1044-1049) can be written with 06 or 16; the alarm setpoints (211-230) only with 16. Writes must also be allowed in the device's write permissions.",
    "32-bit values are high word first. The alarm setpoints have one fixed decimal.",
    "Analog channel values have 1 decimal for temperature sensors; for linear inputs the decimals are those configured for the channel, so the map gives them unscaled.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "tcp",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "port": 502,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
